# Coinbase keys for the crypto book — the ONLY place they live (chmod 600, never committed).
# config.json decides nothing here: whichever file has values is the lane that goes live.
# Leave this whole file commented and the book stays on the shadow ledger (no real money).
#
# PICK ONE LANE — they are different accounts on different hosts, and a key from the wrong host
# answers 401 (the adapter says so in the journal instead of retrying 80 times):
#
# A) Coinbase Exchange  (api.exchange.coinbase.com) — the institutional host, the published
#    maker/taker ladder (0.40/0.60 % under $10 k 30-day volume ... 0.10/0.20 % at $100 k-$1 M).
#    Key minted at exchange.coinbase.com -> Settings -> API with View + Trade, never Transfer.
# COINBASE_MODE=exchange
# COINBASE_API_KEY=
# COINBASE_API_SECRET=
# COINBASE_API_PASSPHRASE=
#
# B) Retail Advanced Trade (api.coinbase.com) — the key from the app's API settings. Its name looks
#    like `organizations/.../apiKeys/...` or `users/.../apiKeys/...`; it signs an ES256 JWT, so put
#    the generated private key in ./coinbase.pem (chmod 600) rather than in this file.
#    Fees are the retail ladder (0.60/1.20 % under $1 k / 30-day): read GET /api/v3/brokerage/
#    transaction_summary and set config.fees to what the account ACTUALLY pays.
# COINBASE_MODE=advanced
# COINBASE_API_KEY=
# COINBASE_CDP_PEM=./coinbase.pem      # ignored — crypto_loop.py loads ./coinbase.pem itself
#
# After any of the above:  launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.hermes.sentry.crypto
# Rehearse first, no money, same payloads:  COINBASE_DRY=1 COINBASE_DRY_EQUITY=20000 python3 run_cycle.py
#
# AND READ config.json before you arm this lane: at Coinbase's fee ladder a 0.5 % stop pays 1.6-2.4 R
# in fees, so the live guard refuses every signal unless this book's `stop_floor_frac` is 0.02 (stop
# widened to 2 %, target scaled by the same factor, R stays R — measured 0.40 R per trade). A Coinbase
# book that does not set the floor is a book that journals refusals.
